        "original_id": "577f00bf-f0b9-55e2-b792-69c121c70e80",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alfred Döblin, César Vallejo\n- Works: Berlin Alexanderplatz, Tales of a Long Night\n- Roles: novelist, essayist, doctor, poet, writer, playwright, journalist\n\nFacts:\n- Alfred Döblin was born on 10 August 1878 and died on 26 June 1957.\n- César Vallejo was born on 16 March 1892 and died on 15 April 1938.\n- Alfred Döblin was a German novelist, essayist, and doctor.\n- César Vallejo was a Peruvian poet, writer, playwright, and journalist.\n- Alfred Döblin is best known for the 1929 novel Berlin Alexanderplatz.\n- Tales of a Long Night, whose German title is Hamlet oder Die lange Nacht nimmt ein Ende, was published in 1956.\n- Tales of a Long Night was the last novel by German author Alfred Döblin.",
